In a trade-idea communication from Martin Zeman (Director, Key Client Partners, Deutsche Bank Wealth Management), his specific AMD options recommendation was to "Buy Aug 17 strike calls for 96c (ref. 16.55, 48d)." His stated rationale was that:
- Replacing the delta (i.e., replacing stock with the calls) protects 5.8% on the downside, which is roughly the implied move;
- The stock has high short interest, so the squeeze potential offers asymmetric risk to the upside;
- The breakeven is about 8.5% away, and the implied move is 5.6%, but the stock has historically moved around 12%, with most big moves to the upside.

This AMD call recommendation appeared alongside similar call-buying ideas for M (Macy's) and ADM in the same note (doc EFTA01387062).

Note: A separate, frequently appearing AMD options transaction in the corpus — selling 200 AMD Oct 13.00 puts at $0.75 (Sept. 20, 2017) — was NOT a Zeman recommendation. That trade was requested/directed by Paul Barrett of Alpha Group Capital and merely executed/reported by Zeman and Vahe Stepanian (docs EFTA01381470, EFTA01434333, EFTA01388027, EFTA01436331, EFTA01427987).
